==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*krep-}}
The {{glossary|adjective}} is {{etydate|1429|nocap=1}}, the {{glossary|noun}} in 1849; from {{inh|en|enm|corporat|corporat(e)|t=({{ng|if a true adjective}}) corporeal, physical, embodied; ({{ng|participle/participial adjective}}) incorporated; corporated, constituted as a legal corporation|pos=used as the past participle of {{m|enm|corporaten}}}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=corporāten|pos=v|id=MED9810}}</ref> from {{der|en|la|corporātus}}, {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|corporō||to make into a body}} (see {{af|en|-ate|id1=adjective|pos1=adjective-forming suffix}}), from {{af|la|corpus|-ō|t1=body|pos1=oblique stem in ''corp-''|id2=denominative|pos2=verb-forming suffix|nocat=1}}. The {{glossary|noun}} was derived by {{glossary|substantivization}} from the {{glossary|adjective}}, see {{af|en|-ate|id1=substantive|pos1=noun-forming suffix}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɔː.pə.ɹət/|/ˈkɔː.pɹət/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-corporate.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkoɹ.pə.ɹət/|/ˈkoɹ.pɹət/|a=GA,CA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkoː.pə.ɹət/|/ˈkoː.pɹət/|a=AU,NZ}}
* {{hyphenation|en|cor|por|ate}}, {{hyphenation|en|corp|orate|nocaption=1}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{senseid|en|of or relating to an institution; institutional}} Of or relating to an [[institution]]; [[institutional]].
#: {{ux|en|The one on Seventh Street is a '''corporate''' franchise.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=w:Edwin Black| title=Internal Combustion| chapter=1| url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL4103950W| passage=But electric vehicles and the batteries that made them run became ensnared in '''corporate''' scandals, fraud, and monopolistic corruption that shook the confidence of the nation and inspired automotive upstarts.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-14|author=w:Jonathan Freedland| volume=189| issue=1| page=18| magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly| title=Obama's once hip brand is now tainted|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/commentisfree/2013/jun/07/obama-apple-google-facebook-tainted-prism| passage=Where we once sent love letters in a sealed envelope, or stuck photographs of our children in a family album, now such private material is despatched to servers and clouds operated by people we don't know and will never meet. Perhaps we assume that our name, address and search preferences will be viewed by some unseen pair of '''corporate''' eyes, probably not human, and don't mind that much.}}
# {{senseid|en|formed into an institution; incorporated}} [[formed|Formed]] into a institution; [[incorporated]].
# {{senseid|en|unified into one entity (collective)}} [[unified|Unified]] into one body; [[collective]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''corporate''' authorship of the working group}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Timon of Athens|II|ii|passage=They answer in a joint and '''corporate''' voice.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:John Eldredge|title=[[w:Wild at Heart (Eldredge book)|Wild at Heart]]|chapter=John Answers Your ''Wild at Heart'' Questions|page=218|publisher=Nelson Books|edition=Expanded|year=2021|origyear=2001|isbn=9781400225262|passage=I believe in the body of Christ, and the regular assembly of believers, the importance of the sacraments, and the need for '''corporate''' worship.}}
# {{senseid|en|soulless}} {{lb|en|colloquial}} [[soulless|Soulless]] and [[inoffensive]]; [[sanitized]] and [[sterile]], like a design from an institution.
#: {{ux|en|It's not that their interior decorating is horrible; it's just that, well, it's so '''corporate'''.}}

